# Compile-time ThreadSanitizer ignorelist (clang -fsanitize-ignorelist; CMakeLists.txt adds it to a clang
# AZURE2_SANITIZE=thread build).  Memory accesses in the listed functions are not instrumented; everything they
# call still is.  It exists for third-party races that a run-time suppression (tsan.supp) cannot silence
# narrowly: a run-time `race:` entry matches any frame of either stack, so suppressing a Minuit2 frame would
# also hide every AZURE2 race in the objective function Minuit2 calls.  Same rule as tsan.supp: third-party code
# only, each entry with its reason.  Format: https://clang.llvm.org/docs/SanitizerSpecialCaseList.html
[thread]

# Minuit2 MnUserFcn::operator() increments its call counter (mutable int MnFcn::fNumCall, MnUserFcn.cxx:21)
# from every thread of the OpenMP numerical gradient (Numerical2PGradientCalculator.cxx:116-163).  Repaired on
# 2026-11-18 by the one listed local change of external/minuit2 (an `omp atomic` increment, here and in
# MnFcn.cxx; docs/source/developer/architecture.rst), so that --max-calls is exact under threads
# (docs/upgrade/fit_threads.md section 3).  The entry is kept until a ThreadSanitizer run without it has passed
# (none was run with the repair); then remove it.
fun:_ZNK4ROOT7Minuit29MnUserFcnclERKNS0_8LAVectorE
